# SHA-256 of gate 5's fixtures — the five deterministic vectors
# sw/board_gate_protocol.py runs against.  16,092 bytes total.
#
# WHY THESE ARE COMMITTED AND HASHED.  Same discipline as GATE4_VECTORS.sha256
# and for the same reason: a board result means nothing unless it can be tied
# to the exact bytes that produced it, and these vectors are GENERATED, so
# regenerating them on the board would let the gate agree with whatever it had
# just made.  The gate refuses to run if the copies it finds do not match.
#
# tb_proto_cases.txt additionally carries a SHA256 row for each of the four
# blobs.  That is not redundant with this file: this record ties the payload to
# the commit, while those rows tie the blobs to THAT manifest, so a manifest
# and a blob from different regenerations cannot be silently combined.
#
# The generator is deterministic and self-checking.  Regenerate with:
#     cd hls/integration && python3 proto_generate_golden.py
# and verify with:
#     sha256sum -c sw/GATE5_VECTORS.sha256      (from the repository root)
#
# Gate 5 is the multi-candidate STREAM PROTOCOL gate: batch TLAST framing,
# per-patch receive re-arming across four different patch sizes, record order,
# extractor re-entry, and the per-kind argmax gate 4's phase D could not test.
